node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Wiki-derived data. Everything under public/ is fetched or generated at setup
# rather than committed, which keeps this repository free of third party content
# entirely. See ATTRIBUTION.md for why that matters: the tiles are Jagex artwork
# that Weird Gloop is permitted to serve (a permission that is not transitive),
# and wiki text is CC BY-NC-SA 3.0, whose NonCommercial clause is not open source
# compatible.
#
# Keeping them out means the code here can carry a clean licence.
#
# This is a blanket rather than a list on purpose. A list only ever covers the
# artifacts that existed when it was written, so the next script to write a new
# folder in here would leak by default. Nothing under public/ is tracked and
# nothing should be. The names it currently holds, for reference: tiles/,
# tiles-clean/, labels.json, mapicons/, mapicons.json.
#
# If a genuine static asset ever needs to ship here, add a negation for that one
# path rather than loosening the blanket. Note that the CI licence gate rejects
# tracked images outright, so a future favicon has to be an inline SVG or a data
# URI in index.html, not a file in here.
public/

# Secrets. There are no accounts, no keys and no server in this project, so
# anything matching these is a mistake rather than a config choice. Cheap
# insurance against the one failure a later commit cannot undo, because history
# is what a clone gets.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx

# Local working notes and agent tooling. The engineering knowledge that is worth
# sharing lives in CONTRIBUTING.md and docs/ instead.
HANDOVER.md
.claude/

# Agent scratch. The audit and handover flows build throwaway harnesses at the
# repository root and are told to delete them afterwards. An ignore rule is a
# stronger guarantee than an instruction, because it survives the agent
# forgetting. Anchored to the root so a real src/check.ts is never shadowed.
/check.ts
/check.mjs
/*.tmp.ts
/*.tmp.mjs
/scratch/

# The Playwright verify harness from CONTRIBUTING.md. Its own node_modules and
# the screenshots it writes, which are renders of third party map artwork and so
# must never be committed. See ATTRIBUTION.md.
/shots/

# Editor state. Holds absolute local paths, which are personal.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# OS noise, both platforms.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini

*.local
*.log
npm-debug.log*
